Consider the following pseudocode:

function push(stack, val):
    stack.append(val)

function pop(stack):
    return stack.removeLast()

What is the time complexity of each operation?

The following pseudocode checks for balanced parentheses:

function isBalanced(s):
    stack = []
    for ch in s:
        if ch in '([{':
            stack.push(ch)
        elif ch in ')]}':
            if stack is empty: return False
            top = stack.pop()
            if not matches(top, ch): return False
    return stack is empty

What is the time and space complexity (n = length of s)?

A stack is implemented using a singly linked list (head = top). What is the complexity of:

function peek(stack):
    return stack.head.value

function size(stack):
    count = 0
    node = stack.head
    while node != null:
        count += 1
        node = node.next
    return count

A stack sorts another stack using only push/pop:

function sortStack(s):
    temp = []
    while s not empty:
        val = s.pop()
        while temp not empty and temp.top() > val:
            s.push(temp.pop())
        temp.push(val)
    return temp

What is the worst-case time complexity?

Consider a simple FIFO queue backed by two stacks (enqueue to stack1, dequeue pops from stack2, refilling from stack1 when empty):

function enqueue(q, val):   // O(?) amortized
    q.s1.push(val)

function dequeue(q):        // O(?) amortized
    if q.s2 is empty:
        while q.s1 not empty:
            q.s2.push(q.s1.pop())
    return q.s2.pop()

What is the amortized complexity of each operation?

Analyse this BFS-style level-order traversal using a queue:

function levelOrder(root):
    if root is null: return
    q = Queue()
    q.enqueue(root)
    while q not empty:
        node = q.dequeue()
        visit(node)
        if node.left: q.enqueue(node.left)
        if node.right: q.enqueue(node.right)

Time and space complexity (n = number of nodes)?

A sliding window maximum uses a monotonic deque:

function maxSlidingWindow(arr, k):
    dq = Deque()   // stores indices; front = max index
    result = []
    for i in 0..n-1:
        while dq not empty and dq.front() < i-k+1:
            dq.popFront()
        while dq not empty and arr[dq.back()] < arr[i]:
            dq.popBack()
        dq.pushBack(i)
        if i >= k-1:
            result.append(arr[dq.front()])
    return result

Time complexity (n = len(arr))?

Postorder traversal using two stacks:

function postorder(root):
    if root is null: return
    s1 = Stack(); s2 = Stack()
    s1.push(root)
    while s1 not empty:
        node = s1.pop()
        s2.push(node)
        if node.left:  s1.push(node.left)
        if node.right: s1.push(node.right)
    while s2 not empty:
        visit(s2.pop())

Time and space complexity?

Morris Inorder Traversal modifies tree links temporarily:

function morrisInorder(root):
    curr = root
    while curr is not null:
        if curr.left is null:
            visit(curr)
            curr = curr.right
        else:
            pred = curr.left
            while pred.right and pred.right != curr:
                pred = pred.right
            if pred.right is null:
                pred.right = curr    // thread
                curr = curr.left
            else:
                pred.right = null   // unthread
                visit(curr)
                curr = curr.right

Time and space complexity?

