Counting total nodes in a complete binary tree (exploiting completeness):

function countNodes(root):
    if root is null: return 0
    lh = leftHeight(root)   // O(log n)
    rh = rightHeight(root)  // O(log n)
    if lh == rh:
        return (1 << lh) - 1   // full subtree: 2^lh - 1
    return 1 + countNodes(root.left) + countNodes(root.right)

Time complexity?

BFS on a tree to find all cousins of a given node (same depth, different parent):

function findCousins(root, target):
    q = Queue(); q.enqueue((root, None))  // (node, parent)
    while q not empty:
        size = q.size(); levelNodes = []
        targetParent = None
        for _ in range(size):
            (node, parent) = q.dequeue()
            if node.val == target: targetParent = parent
            levelNodes.append((node, parent))
            if node.left:  q.enqueue((node.left, node))
            if node.right: q.enqueue((node.right, node))
        if targetParent is not None:
            return [n.val for (n, p) in levelNodes if p != targetParent]
    return []

Time complexity?

In-order successor in a BST (no parent pointer):

function inorderSuccessor(root, target):
    successor = None
    while root is not null:
        if target.val < root.val:
            successor = root
            root = root.left
        else:
            root = root.right
    return successor

